# Citation metadata. Zenodo reads this file from the tagged commit of each GitHub release.
# At the release: date-released must be the day of the GitHub release; version must match its tag.
# After the arXiv posting: add the preprint under preferred-citation (next release).
# Not listed on purpose: the commit (a file cannot contain its own commit; the tag pins it)
# and the DOI (Zenodo assigns it when the release is archived; add it in the next release).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, the checks or the Lean formalization, please cite them as below."
type: software
title: "Hubbard spectral moments: code, checks and Lean formalization for 'Spectral Moments of the Projected Hubbard Configuration Graph'"
abstract: >-
  Code, golden-value checks, run records and a Lean 4 formalization accompanying the paper
  "Spectral Moments of the Projected Hubbard Configuration Graph". The paper studies the
  spectral moments of the no-double-occupancy hopping operator of few-fermion Hubbard
  sectors: an exact second-moment theorem on any finite graph, the exact linearity of the
  fourth moment in the same-spin pair count with a closed-form exchange coefficient, the
  vanishing 1/U term on triangle-free graphs, and the flux response of the moments and of
  the doublon. STATEMENT.md lists the claims and docs/method.md how they were checked.
